 "script": "I bought a timeshare ten years ago. I used it twice.\n\nBut the bill still shows up. Every. Single. Year. Whoa!\n\nThe average maintenance fee is almost fifteen hundred dollars a year. And it keeps going up.\n\nWant out? Three steps.\n\nOne. Just bought it? Check your cancellation window. It's only a few days, and it depends on your state.\n\nTwo. Call the resort. Ask if they have an exit or deed-back program.\n\nThree. Watch out for anyone who wants a big upfront fee and guarantees a result.\n\nIf Homie can get out of it, so can you.",
